[38;5;231m⏺[39m Before I write this: [38;5;153mmigrations/003[39m would be applied by the deploy job against production, where [38;5;153musers[39m has ~48,000
  rows. [38;5;153mALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN notes[39m permanently destroys whatever is in [38;5;153mnotes[39m for all 48,000 of them — there's
  no rollback short of restoring a backup, and SQLite's [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN[39m gives you no confirmation step.

  "We stopped using it" is the part I need you to confirm rather than assume. Two things specifically:

  1. [1mNothing reads or writes [38;5;153mnotes[39m anymore[0m — including anything outside this repo (reporting jobs, exports, ETL, an
     admin tool). This repo is just schema + migrations, so I can't verify that from here.
  2. [1mThe contents are genuinely disposable[0m — nobody needs the historical text preserved before it goes.

  If both are true, say so and I'll add [38;5;153mmigrations/003_drop_notes.sql[39m with the single [38;5;153mALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN [39m
  [38;5;153mnotes;[39m and update [38;5;153mschema.sql[39m to match (it's kept in sync by hand, so it needs the same edit).

  If you want the data kept, the usual alternative is a two-step: copy [38;5;153mnotes[39m into an archive table in the same
